{
  "id": "COMPOUND:31899 - PROTEIN:5821",
  "verbalization": "Nortoxiferine, dihydro- is implicated in the biological pathway leading to MOVP-3 through a series of target relationships, all centered on the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit serves as a common intermediary, with multiple compounds—such as 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol, 5-Oxobrucine, and methyl valerate—acting as targets of this subunit. The evidence suggests that Nortoxiferine, dihydro- may exert its biological effects by modulating the proteasome, which in turn influences the activity of MOVP-3. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Nortoxiferine, dihydro- could regulate proteasome function, thereby affecting the expression or activity of MOVP-3. The recurring involvement of the proteasome and the diverse targets of the subunit suggest a broader role in cellular processes, potentially linking Nortoxiferine, dihydro- to MOVP-3 through a complex, yet interconnected, network of molecular interactions.",
